    "result_text": "The build passes. All changes are complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI unified `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, and removed the standalone `checkDigit`.\n\n**What changed:**\n\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Replaced the `customer_code` column/field and its accessors with `member_id` / `getMemberId`/`setMemberId`. Removed `getMembershipNumber()` and `getCheckDigit()`. Added `fiscalYearSegment(LocalDate)` as the single authority for the 2-digit FY. Rewrote `getFiscalYear()` and `getLocality()` to derive from the `memberId` (parsing the fixed 11-char `<FY><HASH8><CHK>` tail off the end, so the variable-length REGION prefix and any `-<n>` collision suffix are handled). `getOwnerSegment()` now references the memberId transitively through `getLocality()`.\n\n- **`BuildOwner.java`** \u2014 Builds the memberId as `REGION + FY + HASH8 + CHK`, where HASH8 is the same SHA-256-over-(normalizedTelephone+lastName) first-8-hex as the region-and-hash identity, and CHK is a Luhn digit over the digits of `REGION+FY+HASH8`. Collision handling now deduplicates the memberId.\n\n- **`AuditOwnerCreated.java` / `OwnerCreatedEvent.java`** \u2014 The audit line and the structured event now carry the `memberId` (and the audit line reports `fiscalYear`).\n\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Replaced the `customerCode`, `checkDigit`, and `membershipNumber` response fields with a single `memberId`; updated the `fiscalYear` and `locality` descriptions to reference the memberId. (The generated `OwnerDto` and the MapStruct mapping pick this up automatically.)\n\n- **DB schemas** (hsqldb/h2/mysql/postgres) \u2014 Renamed `customer_code` to `member_id` (widened to accommodate the longer format plus collision suffix).\n\nThe acceptance test confirms it end-to-end \u2014 e.g. `memberId=NSW2616E6609E3` (NSW + `26` + `16E6609E` + `3`), with the old `customerCode`/`membershipNumber` fields gone. `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
