    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe refactor is coherent and idiomatic for this codebase:\n\n- **Shared parsing helper.** `memberIdCore()` centralizes the collision-suffix stripping and length guard, and both `getFiscalYear()` and `getLocality()` consume it rather than each re-parsing the raw `memberId`. The `MEMBER_ID_TAIL` constant names the fixed-tail layout so the segment offsets read clearly.\n- **Single FY authority.** `fiscalYearSegment(LocalDate)` is extracted as the one place the FY segment is computed, reused by `BuildOwner` when constructing the id, while `getFiscalYear()` reads it back off the memberId \u2014 which is exactly what the spec (\"the fiscal-year value must reference the memberId\") requires. No duplicated FY logic.\n- **Luhn lands in the right unit.** With the standalone `checkDigit` accessor gone, the Luhn computation moves next to where the id is assembled (`BuildOwner.memberId` \u2192 `luhn`), kept as a focused private static alongside `hash8`/`deduplicate`. It has one caller, so keeping it local (rather than promoting it to a shared util) is the correct altitude \u2014 no over-engineering.\n- **Build vs. parse split is natural.** `BuildOwner` builds `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`; `Owner` exposes derived views by parsing it. That's the existing pattern (builder constructs, entity surfaces `@Transient` derived accessors), not duplication.\n- **Rename propagated consistently** across the entity, audit line, `OwnerCreatedEvent` record, all four schema dialects, and the OpenAPI schema, with javadoc/descriptions updated to match \u2014 nothing left dangling and no class turned into a catch-all.\n\nMinor nit (not blocking): `deduplicate(String code, \u2026)` still names its parameter `code` though it now carries a memberId; the javadoc was updated but the param name wasn't. Not worth a round-trip.",
